      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "In fact, 80% of Anthropic's code is now AI written and this is this stat is at least a few months old.",
      "timestamp_sec": 139,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=139s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "They're seeing 14x the number of commits, which is insane and most of this is AI assisted.",
      "timestamp_sec": 139,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=139s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "It's free for you to produce, free to refactor, and it is not a thing to get hung up on anymore. Humans no longer need to concern themselves with implementation.",
      "timestamp_sec": 247,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=247s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "The important thing is not the code, but the prompt and the guardrails that got you there.",
      "timestamp_sec": 247,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=247s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Agents are actually compounding booboos, which is my word for errors, with zero learning and no bottlenecks and delayed pain.",
      "timestamp_sec": 294,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=294s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Non-critical code, sure, write slop ahead. Critical code, read every line.",
      "timestamp_sec": 338,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=338s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "861% increase in code deletion per PR. So us together with AI agents, we love deleting code.",
      "timestamp_sec": 543,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=543s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Anthropic also said that they're shipping eight times more code per quarter than in 2025.",
      "timestamp_sec": 543,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=543s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Same essay, 31% increase in PRs merged with no review at all, human or agentic. Don't do this. I beg of you.",
      "timestamp_sec": 619,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=619s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Same study, 242% increase in incident per PR. This kind of scary. The second study is also scary. Bugs per developer is up six times than 2025.",
      "timestamp_sec": 619,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=619s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "The continuum is real. It's not about the people. It's about the task.",
      "timestamp_sec": 710,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=710s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "He's not saying don't inspect your code. He's saying inspect the system, not every line.",
      "timestamp_sec": 753,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=753s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "I think the better question right now for all of us is what proof does this specific change need?",
      "timestamp_sec": 830,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=830s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "You read every line of authentication, money movement, permissions, and irreversible data.",
      "timestamp_sec": 868,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=868s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "This is what Ryan Le Popo talks about. Build the system that builds the system because read spends your attention once, engineer makes the system remember.",
      "timestamp_sec": 900,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=900s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "We used to check if Claude is doing the work right. With Fable, we check if Claude is doing the right work.",
      "timestamp_sec": 970,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=970s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "It's never felt so tempting to stop looking at code at all. But don't do this in production.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1009,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=1009s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Capability drift changes where proof belongs. It doesn't remove the requirement of proof.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1048,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=1048s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "But if the builder grades itself, you didn't remove the review, you hid it.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1157,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=1157s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So again, loops don't remove judgment, but they do raise the stakes on where you put it.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1191,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=1191s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Not every line in 2026 needs your eyes. Every system still needs your judgment.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1266,
      "talk_slug": "should-ai-engineers-still-read-code-in-2026-the-zl-continuum",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZpK5PWX2YRM&t=1266s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    }
